  "changelog": "v107: owner-declared VIP correspondents + roster email aliases (issue #44). weights.json gains vip_correspondents (email → label map) and vip_bonus: declared VIPs (e.g. family whose importance volume understates) pin relationship_signal to 1.0, add vip_bonus to the thread total before banding, and are never mined as 'unknown' discoveries — a VIP with no wiki page instead becomes a high-priority discovery_vip candidate. Roster entities may now carry email addresses in aliases: correspondents bind by exact address even when display names share no tokens with the page, so importance marked in the wiki governs scoring on every future excavation. Docs: research.md §7c adds the VIP mechanism, email-alias binding, and the era-bound-volume caveat.",
